1
00:01:08,634 --> 00:01:10,342
Let's go.

2
00:01:17,082 --> 00:01:20,474
You really had no idea
Hongsung had teamed up with Mantua?

3
00:01:20,474 --> 00:01:23,470
No, I never saw it coming.

4
00:01:23,470 --> 00:01:25,654
Look at you bragging.

5
00:01:25,654 --> 00:01:27,254
What's going to happen to us?

6
00:01:27,254 --> 00:01:29,421
What do you mean, what's going to happen?

7
00:01:29,421 --> 00:01:31,834
We used to do business with Hongsung.

8
00:01:31,834 --> 00:01:34,074
We're just going back to the way things were.

9
00:01:34,074 --> 00:01:36,054
Nothing's changing.

10
00:02:41,246 --> 00:02:50,254
[Episode 10,
Even A Lottery Winner Still Goes to Work]

11
00:03:02,854 --> 00:03:04,914
Thank you.

12
00:03:04,914 --> 00:03:08,518
I can't remember the last time
we sat down together like this.

13
00:03:08,518 --> 00:03:11,818
Neither can I. When was it?

14
00:03:11,818 --> 00:03:15,230
I think it was when you were
at the Pyeongtaek branch.

15
00:03:15,230 --> 00:03:17,898
Oh, I suppose it was.

16
00:03:17,898 --> 00:03:20,834
That was when you came to
the Pyeongtaek branch,

17
00:03:20,834 --> 00:03:24,954
and turned the place upside down,
threatening to pull all Hongsung's stores.

18
00:03:26,510 --> 00:03:29,098
Oh, I was shaking in my boots that day.

19
00:03:29,098 --> 00:03:34,121
You kept shouting about pulling the brand out
and complaining to headquarters.

20
00:03:34,121 --> 00:03:36,106
You were so loud

21
00:03:36,106 --> 00:03:39,094
that we ended up getting complaints
from customers, remember?

22
00:03:39,094 --> 00:03:41,298
They said it was too noisy to shop.

23
00:03:41,298 --> 00:03:44,162
Did you know headquarters booked
the room next to the restaurant?

24
00:03:44,162 --> 00:03:45,398
Pardon?

25
00:03:45,398 --> 00:03:49,622
A stenographer will record the minutes
and send them straight to the chairman.

26
00:03:49,622 --> 00:03:52,587
That's how important this meeting is.

27
00:03:52,587 --> 00:03:54,710
Oh, you were there too, weren't you?

28
00:03:54,710 --> 00:03:57,046
Yes, I was there.

29
00:03:57,046 --> 00:04:01,450
After Mr. Hong left, you came back
for the working-level talks,

30
00:04:01,450 --> 00:04:03,002
didn't you, Mr. Jang?

31
00:04:03,002 --> 00:04:05,086
Oh, yes. That's correct.

32
00:04:05,086 --> 00:04:06,130
You remember.

33
00:04:06,130 --> 00:04:09,187
I retrained our staff after that incident.

34
00:04:09,187 --> 00:04:11,514
"Don't you dare mess with Hongsung, got it?"

35
00:04:11,514 --> 00:04:15,154
"Nothing good comes
from crossing them, nothing at all."

36
00:04:16,754 --> 00:04:21,874
Oh, by the way, you heard that
CGM acquired Gwandong, right?

37
00:04:21,874 --> 00:04:23,646
Yeah, I heard about that.

38
00:04:23,646 --> 00:04:26,634
Honestly, it kinda looks desperate.

39
00:04:26,634 --> 00:04:29,590
After their Korean launch flopped,
they can't just leave with nothing.

40
00:04:29,590 --> 00:04:32,770
So they're buying a company just to make it

41
00:04:32,770 --> 00:04:34,654
look like they made it in, right?

42
00:04:34,654 --> 00:04:40,298
Gwandong already carried CGM's products,
so not much has changed.

43
00:04:40,298 --> 00:04:42,246
From Gwandong's point of view,
it's a pretty good deal.

44
00:04:42,246 --> 00:04:43,804
The company was on the verge of collapse,

45
00:04:43,804 --> 00:04:46,470
and they sold their stake at a good price.

46
00:04:46,470 --> 00:04:48,614
CGM really gave a lot of companies
a hard time.

47
00:04:48,614 --> 00:04:51,958
They just pitted us against each other.

48
00:04:51,958 --> 00:04:56,610
It wasn't much of a fight.
We were the only ones taking hits, right?

49
00:04:56,610 --> 00:04:59,954
We didn't even do anything.

50
00:05:07,866 --> 00:05:10,102
Since you brought it up,

51
00:05:10,102 --> 00:05:12,898
this wasn't a fight
between your company and ours.

52
00:05:12,898 --> 00:05:16,462
In fact, pitting the vendors
against each other over the commission rates,

53
00:05:16,462 --> 00:05:18,921
I believe, was your doing.

54
00:05:24,762 --> 00:05:26,914
You're Team Leader Gong Eun Tae, correct?

55
00:05:26,914 --> 00:05:28,558
Yes.

56
00:05:28,558 --> 00:05:31,570
He's the one who brought Mantua
to Korea this time.

57
00:05:31,570 --> 00:05:34,921
Oh, I see.

58
00:05:36,170 --> 00:05:38,810
At the end of the day,
it's business, isn't it?

59
00:05:38,810 --> 00:05:42,918
I hope you understand that we had no choice.

60
00:05:42,918 --> 00:05:45,742
When multiple companies want the same space,

61
00:05:45,742 --> 00:05:48,862
they're bound to compete.

62
00:05:48,862 --> 00:05:51,858
Yes, we fully understand that point.

63
00:05:51,858 --> 00:05:55,454
I'm sure Mr. Gong understands that too.

64
00:05:57,710 --> 00:05:59,718
What I'd like to ask is,

65
00:05:59,718 --> 00:06:03,570
whether Hongsung will take over the brands
Gwandong used to carry,

66
00:06:03,570 --> 00:06:06,594
or leave them with Gwandong.

67
00:06:06,594 --> 00:06:09,446
What's Hongsung's take on this?

68
00:06:09,446 --> 00:06:11,721
[What's Hongsung's take on this?]

69
00:06:13,446 --> 00:06:16,218
We don't plan to take all the brands

70
00:06:16,218 --> 00:06:18,742
that overlap between Mantua and CGM.

71
00:06:18,742 --> 00:06:22,966
Especially if it's a brand they are
already handling in Gwandong.

72
00:06:22,966 --> 00:06:26,674
We don't want Gwandong to disappear either.

73
00:06:26,674 --> 00:06:31,214
The market is more stable
when major players stay in the game.

74
00:06:31,214 --> 00:06:35,662
Oh, I'm glad you see it that way.

75
00:06:35,662 --> 00:06:40,590
As you said, we'd also like to
see Gwandong stay in business.

76
00:06:40,590 --> 00:06:45,254
But I don't quite understand
why you keep bringing up

77
00:06:45,254 --> 00:06:47,970
Gwandong in particular.

78
00:06:47,970 --> 00:06:52,406
As you said, we're also
partly responsible for this situation.

79
00:06:52,406 --> 00:06:57,921
We'd like to prevent
any unnecessary competition.

80
00:06:59,378 --> 00:07:03,186
<i>Of course, Hongsung won't go along with us.</i>

81
00:07:03,186 --> 00:07:06,382
That's why we should strike first.

82
00:07:06,382 --> 00:07:10,602
But what if Hongsung
actually pulls all its stores?

83
00:07:10,602 --> 00:07:12,189
No matter how big Hongsung is,

84
00:07:12,189 --> 00:07:14,922
how is it supposed to sell clothes
without department stores?

85
00:07:14,922 --> 00:07:16,787
We need to come down hard.

86
00:07:17,442 --> 00:07:22,938
Look, if this blows up,
it's over for both of us.

87
00:07:22,938 --> 00:07:25,021
Just do something.

88
00:07:26,710 --> 00:07:28,754
So, here's what we're thinking.

89
00:07:28,754 --> 00:07:32,670
For the brands that overlap between
Hongsung and Gwandong in our select shop,

90
00:07:32,670 --> 00:07:36,986
how about we source
a few of them from Gwandong too?

91
00:07:36,986 --> 00:07:38,854
What do you think?

92
00:07:46,122 --> 00:07:48,621
What do you think, Mr. Gong?

93
00:07:50,386 --> 00:07:52,521
Oh, personally,

94
00:07:53,230 --> 00:07:55,962
I'd ask you to reconsider that.

95
00:07:55,962 --> 00:07:58,502
Pardon? May I ask why you feel that way?

96
00:07:58,502 --> 00:08:00,194
You're our client,

97
00:08:00,194 --> 00:08:03,126
so it's not our place
to tell you what to decide.

98
00:08:03,126 --> 00:08:08,287
But the people at Mantua
aren't exactly reasonable.

99
00:08:08,287 --> 00:08:12,602
So, are you saying Hongsung is fine,
but Mantua isn't?

100
00:08:12,602 --> 00:08:15,750
Yes, because your company
is already in China.

101
00:08:15,750 --> 00:08:17,806
If CGM tries to use Gwandong

102
00:08:17,806 --> 00:08:21,150
as a backdoor to enter
your Chinese department stores,

103
00:08:21,150 --> 00:08:24,090
I don't think Mantua
would just sit back and watch.

104
00:08:24,090 --> 00:08:27,182
If that happens, the traditional
European luxury brands on the first floor

105
00:08:27,182 --> 00:08:32,330
might end up completely empty.

106
00:08:32,330 --> 00:08:35,138
Ms. Park and I will go with the flow.

107
00:08:35,138 --> 00:08:37,070
Mr. Jang, you just set the tone.

108
00:08:37,070 --> 00:08:38,790
I'll leave the fighting to you, Mr. Gong.

109
00:08:38,790 --> 00:08:40,042
Yes, understood, sir.

110
00:08:40,042 --> 00:08:42,118
- Mr. Gong.
- Yes.

111
00:08:42,118 --> 00:08:44,682
Go wild, do whatever you want.

112
00:08:44,682 --> 00:08:46,538
Understood, sir.

113
00:08:46,538 --> 00:08:50,158
And if you plan to diversify your supply
through Gwandong,

114
00:08:50,158 --> 00:08:54,386
we'll revert your store-entry commission
to the standard rate.

115
00:08:54,386 --> 00:08:56,478
I hope you can understand this point.

116
00:08:56,478 --> 00:09:00,054
Wait, wasn't that Hongsung's offer
in the first place?

117
00:09:00,054 --> 00:09:01,725
The original contract

118
00:09:01,725 --> 00:09:04,974
was for your select shops
to carry only Hongsung's products.

119
00:09:04,974 --> 00:09:09,454
If you're changing the terms,
shouldn't we change ours as well?

120
00:09:09,454 --> 00:09:14,050
And we'll lower our commission to 14%
for luxury brands.

121
00:09:14,050 --> 00:09:15,714
Wait, 14%?

122
00:09:15,714 --> 00:09:18,318
I believe you were charging 16% before,

123
00:09:18,318 --> 00:09:21,450
and after all this CGM trouble,
you jacked it up to 20%.

124
00:09:21,450 --> 00:09:23,634
You even demanded 22% from CGM.

125
00:09:23,634 --> 00:09:26,262
If you want to start
carrying our products again,

126
00:09:26,262 --> 00:09:28,898
you'll have to match our 14%.

127
00:09:28,898 --> 00:09:30,802
Wait, that's a bit...

128
00:09:30,802 --> 00:09:35,758
We understand what your company did to us.

129
00:09:35,758 --> 00:09:39,366
So we'd appreciate the same
understanding from you.

130
00:09:39,366 --> 00:09:41,687
At the end of the day, it's all business.

131
00:10:00,394 --> 00:10:03,146
- Oh, Manager!
- How are you?

132
00:10:03,146 --> 00:10:05,238
Mr. Yang!

133
00:10:05,850 --> 00:10:07,987
Enjoy it nice and cold.

134
00:10:09,498 --> 00:10:12,190
What on earth is going on?

135
00:10:12,190 --> 00:10:15,278
Why keep pulling stores in and out
when we were doing fine?

136
00:10:15,278 --> 00:10:18,530
Well, you know how business goes sometimes.

137
00:10:18,530 --> 00:10:21,790
It's fine if Paradis Mall and Hongsung
are playing tug-of-war,

138
00:10:21,790 --> 00:10:25,066
but aren't we the ones
having to move the merchandise around?

139
00:10:25,066 --> 00:10:26,914
I know, I know, Manager.

140
00:10:26,914 --> 00:10:28,678
That's why I'm working on something.

141
00:10:28,678 --> 00:10:30,290
When we renew the contract this time,

142
00:10:30,290 --> 00:10:34,542
I'm going to try to raise
the managers' commissions.

143
00:10:34,542 --> 00:10:38,630
- Are you serious?
- I may be a bit of a pain, but not a liar.

144
00:10:38,630 --> 00:10:40,922
Yeah, that's true.

145
00:10:40,922 --> 00:10:43,987
Oh, this should probably be changed.

146
00:10:44,810 --> 00:10:46,754
Alright, there we go.

147
00:10:53,246 --> 00:10:55,238
- Mr. Yang.
- Yeah?

148
00:10:55,238 --> 00:10:57,054
Over there...

149
00:11:09,242 --> 00:11:12,421
What? Do you want to say something?

150
00:11:14,362 --> 00:11:17,330
If you have nothing to say, just go.
I'm swamped here.

151
00:11:17,330 --> 00:11:19,187
I'm sorry!

152
00:11:22,046 --> 00:11:23,486
For what?

153
00:11:23,486 --> 00:11:26,554
Well, I mean...

154
00:11:26,554 --> 00:11:27,926
What exactly are you sorry for?

155
00:11:27,926 --> 00:11:29,190
Well, you know...

156
00:11:29,190 --> 00:11:32,630
I must've lost my head for a moment.

157
00:11:32,630 --> 00:11:33,974
I mean...

158
00:11:33,974 --> 00:11:38,978
As you know, when we opened the store,
we relied heavily on Hongsung.

159
00:11:38,978 --> 00:11:42,250
I think I unconsciously felt we were always
bending over backward for Hongsung.

160
00:11:42,250 --> 00:11:47,550
And I guess I let
a lot of resentment build up.

161
00:11:47,550 --> 00:11:50,466
I understand why you were upset.

162
00:11:50,466 --> 00:11:52,621
I hope you can let it go!

163
00:11:56,510 --> 00:11:59,462
Well, first of all,
thank you for apologizing.

164
00:11:59,462 --> 00:12:02,338
I wasn't exactly blameless either.

165
00:12:02,338 --> 00:12:06,754
Why don't we just call it even
for that mess and move on?

166
00:12:06,754 --> 00:12:10,086
Oh, thank you. I really appreciate it.

167
00:12:10,086 --> 00:12:12,854
Oh, wait! In that case...

168
00:12:13,778 --> 00:12:19,454
Can we assume the contract
will proceed as before?

169
00:12:20,554 --> 00:12:22,054
No, that's not happening.

170
00:12:22,054 --> 00:12:24,214
- Pardon?
- We yelled and fought each other.

171
00:12:24,214 --> 00:12:27,386
I totally admit it, I was completely wrong.

172
00:12:27,386 --> 00:12:30,854
But the way Paradis Mall treated us back then

173
00:12:31,538 --> 00:12:33,714
was clearly out of line.

174
00:12:33,714 --> 00:12:36,254
Of course, contracts can always be renewed,

175
00:12:36,254 --> 00:12:39,746
and you can take advantage of
a favorable situation.

176
00:12:39,746 --> 00:12:41,950
But the way you did it was too much.

177
00:12:41,950 --> 00:12:44,366
You can go now. I've got a lot of work to do.

178
00:12:44,366 --> 00:12:47,538
Please, I'm begging you, Mr. Yang.

179
00:12:47,538 --> 00:12:50,490
We also agreed to split

180
00:12:50,490 --> 00:12:55,150
the penalty payment to Hongsung
50/50 with CGM.

181
00:12:55,150 --> 00:12:58,787
At this rate, our company
is really going under!

182
00:12:59,518 --> 00:13:02,466
That's for Paradis Mall to deal with.

183
00:13:02,466 --> 00:13:04,270
Companies don't go under that easily.

184
00:13:04,270 --> 00:13:05,922
I know. You won't go under.

185
00:13:05,922 --> 00:13:07,694
Mr. Yang!

186
00:13:07,694 --> 00:13:10,554
Please, I'm begging you.

187
00:13:11,322 --> 00:13:13,838
Oh, for god's sake!

188
00:13:13,838 --> 00:13:17,154
I'll even help carry boxes for you.

189
00:13:17,946 --> 00:13:20,050
Why would you carry boxes?

190
00:13:20,050 --> 00:13:22,630
Why would we make you do something so menial?

191
00:13:22,630 --> 00:13:24,050
Oh, jeez.

192
00:13:24,050 --> 00:13:27,302
Well, I noticed the store's interior
looked pretty dated.

193
00:13:27,302 --> 00:13:31,126
Let's talk again
about the interior design. Okay?

194
00:13:31,126 --> 00:13:32,994
Later, later.
You can get on your knees later.

195
00:13:32,994 --> 00:13:34,287
No, no, later! I'll call you later.

196
00:13:34,287 --> 00:13:35,987
Oh, you're so heavy.

197
00:13:36,602 --> 00:13:39,387
Oh, okay. I'll call you.

198
00:13:40,770 --> 00:13:42,822
Jeez.

199
00:13:42,822 --> 00:13:46,121
Wait, Mr. Yang...

200
00:13:50,258 --> 00:13:52,134
Seriously...

201
00:13:53,638 --> 00:13:55,754
Darn it!

202
00:14:16,558 --> 00:14:17,930
Good work, everyone.

203
00:14:17,930 --> 00:14:19,374
Thank you for your hard work.

204
00:14:19,374 --> 00:14:21,014
Ms. Park, come up to my office.

205
00:14:21,014 --> 00:14:22,818
Yes, sir.

206
00:14:26,814 --> 00:14:28,026
Oh, dear.

207
00:14:28,026 --> 00:14:30,614
Go on ahead.
I'll park the car and be right in.

208
00:14:30,614 --> 00:14:32,762
Alright.

209
00:14:32,762 --> 00:14:34,686
Good work.

210
00:15:04,866 --> 00:15:07,054
How did you get up here?

211
00:15:07,958 --> 00:15:09,178
It still works.

212
00:15:09,178 --> 00:15:10,970
[Jung Sun Hyuk]

213
00:15:13,287 --> 00:15:15,882
Strangely, I wanted to come up here.

214
00:15:15,882 --> 00:15:18,354
You have a nicer office now.

215
00:15:21,221 --> 00:15:24,886
I heard CGM acquired Gwandong.

216
00:15:24,886 --> 00:15:27,054
Are you working at Gwandong?

217
00:15:28,098 --> 00:15:29,842
America is great, I'll give them that.

218
00:15:29,842 --> 00:15:33,038
Even after I screwed things up that badly,
they gave me another chance.

219
00:15:33,038 --> 00:15:35,842
So I'll be working at Gwandong for a while.

220
00:15:35,842 --> 00:15:37,721
That's great.

221
00:15:39,454 --> 00:15:42,718
You landed Mantua, didn't you?

222
00:15:42,718 --> 00:15:44,074
My team did it.

223
00:15:44,074 --> 00:15:47,122
Stop saying it like that.
It's not a good look.

224
00:15:47,122 --> 00:15:49,487
You can just say you did it.

225
00:15:50,478 --> 00:15:53,350
Hongsung seems to have tightened
its grip on the market.

226
00:15:53,350 --> 00:15:58,638
I saw you actually gave up some margin
to the companies that stayed loyal.

227
00:15:58,638 --> 00:16:01,986
You sent a clear signal to the market.

228
00:16:01,986 --> 00:16:05,154
"Stick with Hongsung and you profit."

229
00:16:05,154 --> 00:16:08,602
"Go against Hongsung, and we'll
fight back with everything we've got."

230
00:16:10,042 --> 00:16:12,222
Well, that wasn't really our intention.

231
00:16:12,222 --> 00:16:16,354
We were just expressing
our gratitude in our own way.

232
00:16:17,798 --> 00:16:19,814
Honestly, you had fun, didn't you?

233
00:16:19,814 --> 00:16:21,187
With what?

234
00:16:21,187 --> 00:16:23,238
The work.

235
00:16:23,238 --> 00:16:25,310
You enjoyed it, didn't you?

236
00:16:25,310 --> 00:16:27,226
I can tell without asking.

237
00:16:27,226 --> 00:16:30,021
I even had fun though I lost.

238
00:16:31,594 --> 00:16:35,486
Leaving Hongsung makes me
feel like I'm working again.

239
00:16:35,486 --> 00:16:38,806
So I don't really regret it.

240
00:16:38,806 --> 00:16:42,554
Why? Because I genuinely enjoy it.

241
00:16:43,254 --> 00:16:47,542
That's why I'm so jealous of you.

242
00:16:47,542 --> 00:16:52,287
It took me leaving to find it,
but you found it without leaving.

243
00:16:54,078 --> 00:16:58,534
I do enjoy the work.

244
00:16:58,534 --> 00:17:02,787
But I think my takeaway is a bit different.

245
00:17:03,654 --> 00:17:07,166
As you said, the company
went through a major crisis,

246
00:17:07,166 --> 00:17:10,454
and I enjoyed overcoming it.

247
00:17:11,422 --> 00:17:15,470
<i>Besides the excitement of the job itself,</i>

248
00:17:15,470 --> 00:17:18,998
<i>I felt incredibly lonely when I got home.</i>

249
00:17:18,998 --> 00:17:22,886
<i>How should I put it?
If I'm being a bit dramatic,</i>

250
00:17:22,886 --> 00:17:26,987
<i>it felt like I saved the world
and nobody even knew.</i>

251
00:17:28,002 --> 00:17:29,682
<i>That's how life is, I guess.</i>

252
00:17:29,682 --> 00:17:32,921
<i>What's important to me
isn't necessarily important to others.</i>

253
00:17:34,338 --> 00:17:36,314
<i>But then, out of nowhere,</i>

254
00:17:37,818 --> 00:17:40,721
I suddenly started missing everyone
from the office so much.

255
00:17:41,590 --> 00:17:43,987
Come on, I'm serious.

256
00:17:45,010 --> 00:17:46,887
We know, right?

257
00:17:47,602 --> 00:17:49,746
<i>What we did</i>

258
00:17:49,746 --> 00:17:51,854
<i>and how we did it.</i>

259
00:17:51,854 --> 00:17:56,087
<i>How we came up with ideas
and how much we agonized over them.</i>

260
00:17:57,254 --> 00:18:01,021
<i>How we fought and negotiated.</i>

261
00:18:04,366 --> 00:18:06,966
<i>How anxious we were.</i>

262
00:18:06,966 --> 00:18:09,121
<i>How hard it was,</i>

263
00:18:09,986 --> 00:18:12,087
<i>and how happy we were.</i>

264
00:18:14,110 --> 00:18:18,821
I realized how grateful I am
to have colleagues who share it all with me.

265
00:18:19,910 --> 00:18:22,114
So these days,

266
00:18:22,114 --> 00:18:24,021
I just enjoy that feeling.

267
00:18:25,662 --> 00:18:27,738
Eun Tae,

268
00:18:29,014 --> 00:18:31,487
was I ever that kind of person for you?

269
00:18:37,182 --> 00:18:41,894
I don't think you ever
have to cut someone off.

270
00:18:41,894 --> 00:18:47,087
I think the right distance changes
with time and people.

271
00:18:48,770 --> 00:18:50,486
Sometime later,

272
00:18:50,486 --> 00:18:52,921
once a bit more time has passed,

273
00:18:52,921 --> 00:18:57,821
let's grab a drink, just like we used to.
How about it?

274
00:18:59,786 --> 00:19:01,262
Sounds good, Mr. Jung.

275
00:19:01,262 --> 00:19:02,654
Good.

276
00:19:02,654 --> 00:19:04,530
Darn it.

277
00:19:04,530 --> 00:19:05,978
Mind if I have another cigarette?

278
00:19:05,978 --> 00:19:08,262
Why are you asking me for permission?

279
00:19:08,262 --> 00:19:10,087
It's your company.

280
00:19:15,914 --> 00:19:18,121
- Mr. Jung.
- Yeah?

281
00:19:18,782 --> 00:19:21,921
Do you still play the lottery?

282
00:19:23,222 --> 00:19:25,150
Do you?

283
00:19:31,530 --> 00:19:33,938
Honestly, wasn't that a bit much?

284
00:19:33,938 --> 00:19:37,514
I understand security is important,
but shutting me out like that?

285
00:19:37,514 --> 00:19:39,346
I'm sorry, sir.

286
00:19:40,462 --> 00:19:42,186
Don't be.

287
00:19:42,186 --> 00:19:44,987
You'd do the exact same thing
all over again, wouldn't you?

288
00:19:45,962 --> 00:19:48,330
Jeez, seriously.

289
00:19:48,330 --> 00:19:50,262
How old is your kid now?

290
00:19:50,262 --> 00:19:52,154
She's in high school.

291
00:19:53,322 --> 00:19:55,887
You did a great job raising her
while working so hard.

292
00:19:55,887 --> 00:19:58,002
I didn't do much.

293
00:19:58,002 --> 00:19:59,514
She pretty much raised herself.

294
00:19:59,514 --> 00:20:02,562
You'll need to make good money
to send her to college.

295
00:20:02,562 --> 00:20:06,121
Yes. That's why I work hard.

296
00:20:06,926 --> 00:20:10,446
You know executives get
full tuition for their kids, right?

297
00:20:10,446 --> 00:20:12,426
Pardon?

298
00:20:15,598 --> 00:20:17,542
Let's go for the director position.

299
00:20:20,978 --> 00:20:23,250
We'll merge Sales Divisions 1 and 2

300
00:20:23,250 --> 00:20:25,438
and create a Sales Director position.

301
00:20:25,438 --> 00:20:27,354
You'll also have a Sales Planning Department
reporting directly to you.

302
00:20:27,354 --> 00:20:30,518
[Organizational Restructuring,
Personnel Changes]

303
00:20:30,518 --> 00:20:33,082
Go on, give it your best.

304
00:20:33,082 --> 00:20:34,854
Understood, sir.

305
00:20:35,474 --> 00:20:37,174
Hey.

306
00:20:37,174 --> 00:20:38,666
Yes?

307
00:20:38,666 --> 00:20:40,654
Aren't you going to say thank you?

308
00:20:43,086 --> 00:20:45,382
Thank you, sir.

309
00:20:45,382 --> 00:20:47,387
Jeez.

310
00:20:52,582 --> 00:20:55,254
[HR Notice, Personnel Changes
and Organizational Restructuring]

311
00:21:00,050 --> 00:21:01,742
[Personnel Changes]

312
00:21:01,742 --> 00:21:05,087
[Gong Eun Tae,
Deputy Director of Sales Strategy]

313
00:21:14,598 --> 00:21:18,026
Congratulations, Mr. Gong.

314
00:21:18,026 --> 00:21:19,826
Mr. Yang,

315
00:21:20,454 --> 00:21:21,898
congratulations.

316
00:21:21,898 --> 00:21:23,698
What?

317
00:21:24,421 --> 00:21:28,387
[Yang Jun Ho, Sales Manager]

318
00:21:54,990 --> 00:21:56,094
Congratulations, Mr. Oh.

319
00:21:56,094 --> 00:21:57,606
Oh, no.

320
00:21:57,606 --> 00:22:01,987
Oh, I'm absolutely the type
to get all worked up over a promotion.

321
00:22:01,987 --> 00:22:03,578
- Jeez.
- Oh, my.

322
00:22:03,578 --> 00:22:06,150
- Congratulations!
- What's there to congratulate me for?

323
00:22:06,150 --> 00:22:08,454
- I really mean it. Congratulations.
- No, no.

324
00:22:08,454 --> 00:22:09,922
Congratulations, Deputy Director.

325
00:22:09,922 --> 00:22:12,287
- Oh, thank you.
- Congratulations.

326
00:22:15,766 --> 00:22:17,654
Everyone in Sales Team 5,

327
00:22:18,422 --> 00:22:20,954
you've got ten minutes to wrap up your work.

328
00:22:30,338 --> 00:22:33,830
Oh, Deputy Director Gong,
let me make you a drink this time.

329
00:22:33,830 --> 00:22:36,738
Wait, you shouldn't be doing this.

330
00:22:36,738 --> 00:22:39,686
Come on, I'll make the drink you like...

331
00:22:39,686 --> 00:22:41,622
Oh, what the heck?
We're out of all the cold stuff.

332
00:22:41,622 --> 00:22:42,902
I'll go grab some, Team Leader Yang.

333
00:22:42,902 --> 00:22:44,728
Ji Hye, you need to grill the meat.

334
00:22:44,728 --> 00:22:46,546
Why are you trying to do everything yourself?

335
00:22:46,546 --> 00:22:48,098
Gi Tae, what are you doing right now?

336
00:22:48,098 --> 00:22:50,366
Team Leader, let me just finish this,
and I'll go get them.

337
00:22:50,366 --> 00:22:51,434
I'll do it, Team Leader.

338
00:22:51,434 --> 00:22:53,674
Oh, Team Leader, please sit down.
It's all done, all done.

339
00:22:53,674 --> 00:22:56,078
She's an assistant manager.
The team leader is right here.

340
00:22:56,078 --> 00:22:58,378
Oh, I'm sorry, Team Leader.

341
00:22:58,378 --> 00:23:00,770
Oh, come on!

342
00:23:00,770 --> 00:23:03,154
Deputy Director, please!

343
00:23:14,678 --> 00:23:16,722
Here, take this. You said it's good
for your stomach.

344
00:23:16,722 --> 00:23:19,487
[Stomach Health Supplement]

345
00:23:25,986 --> 00:23:28,910
After all these years at the company,
I guess I've earned a day like this.

346
00:23:28,910 --> 00:23:31,514
There really aren't any days
when everything is just good.

347
00:23:31,514 --> 00:23:33,174
I know.

348
00:23:33,174 --> 00:23:35,434
Our team really did well, didn't we?

349
00:23:35,434 --> 00:23:37,230
Well, this is all because of...

350
00:23:38,290 --> 00:23:39,474
It's all thanks to you, Team Leader.

351
00:23:39,474 --> 00:23:42,574
Oh, please, it's thanks to you,
Deputy Director.

352
00:23:42,574 --> 00:23:46,221
Wow, this is hilarious,
just us talking like this.

353
00:23:47,550 --> 00:23:53,206
I think all of this happened
because you got mad at me that day.

354
00:23:53,206 --> 00:23:57,986
Come to think of it,
our team's success started then too.

355
00:23:57,986 --> 00:24:01,910
If you hadn't gotten mad at me that day

356
00:24:01,910 --> 00:24:04,158
and just let it slide,

357
00:24:04,158 --> 00:24:06,942
I don't think we'd be here now.

358
00:24:06,942 --> 00:24:09,787
Thank you for getting mad at me.

359
00:24:16,174 --> 00:24:18,146
By the way,

360
00:24:18,146 --> 00:24:20,446
what will happen to Ji Hye?

361
00:24:20,446 --> 00:24:22,550
Our team's results are good,

362
00:24:22,550 --> 00:24:25,786
and her team leader's review
should be good too.

363
00:24:25,786 --> 00:24:27,390
But I'm still worried.

364
00:24:27,390 --> 00:24:30,790
I've talked to the other team leaders,

365
00:24:30,790 --> 00:24:32,430
but I don't know how it'll turn out.

366
00:24:32,430 --> 00:24:34,521
Oh, it's done. Here, eat.

367
00:24:35,806 --> 00:24:38,970
We've done everything we can,
so we just have to wait and see.

368
00:24:38,970 --> 00:24:40,922
Isn't there anything we can do?

369
00:24:40,922 --> 00:24:43,254
I just can't put my mind at ease.

370
00:25:02,550 --> 00:25:04,470
Keep up the good work.

371
00:25:04,470 --> 00:25:08,882
- What brings you here?
- I'm supposed to meet someone inside here.

372
00:25:08,882 --> 00:25:11,587
You can't just walk in here like this.

373
00:25:24,170 --> 00:25:26,890
Yes, this is the Executive Director's office.

374
00:25:26,890 --> 00:25:28,090
Yes.

375
00:25:28,090 --> 00:25:29,954
Wait, what?

376
00:25:34,166 --> 00:25:35,930
Seriously, he's...

377
00:25:38,742 --> 00:25:41,954
- CEO?
- What? Why are you working?

378
00:25:41,954 --> 00:25:44,430
Well, it's work hours.
What else would I be doing?

379
00:25:44,430 --> 00:25:49,090
You could've practiced putting.
Then my visit would've been worth it.

380
00:25:49,090 --> 00:25:52,354
I put it away in case you came.

381
00:25:52,354 --> 00:25:53,830
Get me a cup of coffee.

382
00:25:53,830 --> 00:25:55,582
Sure. What kind of coffee would you like?

383
00:25:55,582 --> 00:25:58,242
Ethiopian Yirgacheffe.

384
00:25:58,242 --> 00:25:59,454
Just give him an instant coffee.

385
00:25:59,454 --> 00:26:01,250
Yes, sir.

386
00:26:02,662 --> 00:26:05,050
What brings you here without notice?

387
00:26:05,050 --> 00:26:07,614
Why would I call
before coming to my own company?

388
00:26:07,614 --> 00:26:09,842
It just puts me on edge.

389
00:26:09,842 --> 00:26:10,974
Fair point.

390
00:26:10,974 --> 00:26:12,750
Yeah.

391
00:26:13,430 --> 00:26:15,458
I saw the personnel changes.

392
00:26:15,458 --> 00:26:17,618
There were the issues with Sales Division 2,

393
00:26:17,618 --> 00:26:19,262
and the Mantua order situation,

394
00:26:19,262 --> 00:26:21,510
so I made the changes with the restructuring.

395
00:26:21,510 --> 00:26:24,238
Companies are really something else, huh?

396
00:26:24,238 --> 00:26:28,762
Just when you think everything's perfect
and you don't need to touch a thing,

397
00:26:28,762 --> 00:26:31,514
a problem comes up.

398
00:26:31,514 --> 00:26:32,666
That's because people run them.

399
00:26:32,666 --> 00:26:35,222
Yeah, but then again,

400
00:26:35,222 --> 00:26:37,787
when you think it's all over,
and there's no coming back,

401
00:26:37,787 --> 00:26:41,750
somehow, some way, things work out.

402
00:26:41,750 --> 00:26:43,126
That's because people run them.

403
00:26:43,126 --> 00:26:45,187
I suppose that's true.

404
00:26:45,890 --> 00:26:49,002
By the way, is that Team Leader Gong
any good?

405
00:26:49,002 --> 00:26:50,958
I'm keeping a close eye on him.

406
00:26:50,958 --> 00:26:54,454
I'd like to meet him. Send him up.

407
00:26:57,670 --> 00:26:59,554
- Gong Eun Tae!
- Yes?

408
00:26:59,554 --> 00:27:00,762
The CEO wants to see you.

409
00:27:00,762 --> 00:27:03,282
- Pardon?
- The CEO asked for you. Get up here fast.

410
00:27:03,282 --> 00:27:05,054
Oh, yes, sir.

411
00:27:09,158 --> 00:27:11,987
But why would the CEO want to see me?

412
00:27:12,614 --> 00:27:14,962
How would I know?

413
00:27:14,962 --> 00:27:17,390
What, are you nervous?

414
00:27:17,390 --> 00:27:21,087
No, but you seem to be the one who's nervous.

415
00:27:23,262 --> 00:27:25,202
Have you ever met the CEO?

416
00:27:25,202 --> 00:27:28,046
No. I only saw him from a distance
at the New Year's party.

417
00:27:28,046 --> 00:27:29,862
He never comes to the office, right?

418
00:27:29,862 --> 00:27:31,590
Yes, that's what I've heard.

419
00:27:31,590 --> 00:27:36,187
I've never known him to show up
unannounced and call someone in.

420
00:27:36,846 --> 00:27:38,650
This is a first.

421
00:27:41,870 --> 00:27:45,221
Have you ever met him, sir?

422
00:27:47,758 --> 00:27:49,926
Once, during a strategy meeting
for the duty-free business.

423
00:27:49,926 --> 00:27:51,782
What was he like?

424
00:27:53,942 --> 00:27:57,562
At first, he came off
as a bit sloppy, I guess.

425
00:27:57,562 --> 00:28:01,038
But as the meeting went on, I realized,

426
00:28:01,038 --> 00:28:04,287
he is not the kind of man I can ever judge.

427
00:28:07,266 --> 00:28:10,742
Take it easy. You're as good as dead anyway.

428
00:28:10,742 --> 00:28:12,954
<i>Door opens.</i>

429
00:28:16,206 --> 00:28:18,086
Go on in.

430
00:28:39,406 --> 00:28:40,994
Is that him?

431
00:28:40,994 --> 00:28:43,210
- Yes, sir.
- Yeah.

432
00:28:43,210 --> 00:28:45,042
Come on in, please.

433
00:28:47,110 --> 00:28:48,866
Right over here.

434
00:28:48,866 --> 00:28:50,782
Oh, yes, sir.

435
00:29:05,202 --> 00:29:07,618
You're quite a fine-looking young man!

436
00:29:07,618 --> 00:29:10,442
Oh, thank you, sir.

437
00:29:10,442 --> 00:29:12,487
I hear you've been working hard.

438
00:29:12,487 --> 00:29:14,610
Congrats on the promotion to Deputy Director.

439
00:29:14,610 --> 00:29:16,794
Thank you, sir.

440
00:29:16,794 --> 00:29:21,058
You know I don't come
to the office much, right?

441
00:29:23,021 --> 00:29:26,042
I heard you have more important things
to do outside the office.

442
00:29:26,042 --> 00:29:29,014
Oh, you sweet talker.

443
00:29:29,014 --> 00:29:31,698
No, I'm just playing around.

444
00:29:31,698 --> 00:29:36,358
I didn't come here
because I got bored of having fun.

445
00:29:36,358 --> 00:29:39,874
I wanted to give you a gift, Mr. Gong.

446
00:29:39,874 --> 00:29:42,706
From what I've heard, you deserve one.

447
00:29:42,706 --> 00:29:46,558
Pick out a promotion gift for yourself.

448
00:29:46,558 --> 00:29:48,946
What kind of gift are you talking about, sir?

449
00:29:48,946 --> 00:29:51,987
Anything within my authority.

450
00:30:22,090 --> 00:30:23,998
Mr. Gong,

451
00:30:25,198 --> 00:30:27,154
what did he call you in for?

452
00:30:29,594 --> 00:30:32,070
<i>Oh, just tell me. Anything at all.</i>

453
00:30:32,070 --> 00:30:34,362
Anything's fine. Really.

454
00:30:34,362 --> 00:30:36,821
Are you sure that's okay, sir?

455
00:30:41,870 --> 00:30:43,662
Sir,

456
00:30:43,662 --> 00:30:48,126
we have a contract employee named Lee Ji Hye.

457
00:30:48,126 --> 00:30:50,402
If I can really

458
00:30:50,402 --> 00:30:52,578
choose my gift,

459
00:30:52,578 --> 00:30:55,921
I'd like to make her a permanent employee.

460
00:30:58,538 --> 00:31:02,810
Is this Ms. Lee Ji Hye good at her job?

461
00:31:02,810 --> 00:31:08,387
Yes, sir. She played a big part
in securing our contract with Mantua.

462
00:31:10,334 --> 00:31:13,221
So she's good at her job, huh?

463
00:31:14,994 --> 00:31:16,962
That's a shame.

464
00:31:18,926 --> 00:31:24,002
Someone that good would've
become permanent without you asking.

465
00:31:24,002 --> 00:31:27,254
- Sir.
- Oh, hold on.

466
00:31:28,687 --> 00:31:30,350
Mr. Gong, listen carefully.

467
00:31:30,350 --> 00:31:31,586
Yes, sir.

468
00:31:31,586 --> 00:31:33,462
I'm going to

469
00:31:34,238 --> 00:31:36,521
fire her.

470
00:31:46,734 --> 00:31:50,854
[HR, Contract Termination Notice Posted]

471
00:31:55,221 --> 00:32:02,187
[Notice of Contract Termination, Lee Ji Hye]

472
00:32:04,126 --> 00:32:06,921
What is that supposed to mean?

473
00:32:07,526 --> 00:32:11,518
I gave you authority, Mr. Gong.

474
00:32:11,518 --> 00:32:15,530
That was your first task
as a Deputy Director.

475
00:32:15,530 --> 00:32:17,487
You could've used that authority

476
00:32:17,487 --> 00:32:20,170
to change unfair policies

477
00:32:20,170 --> 00:32:22,218
or restructure the organization.

478
00:32:22,218 --> 00:32:25,798
You could've given Sales
the authority to handle matters

479
00:32:25,798 --> 00:32:29,421
that once required
Finance and Legal approval.

480
00:32:29,421 --> 00:32:35,666
And all you did with that authority
was make a contract worker permanent?

481
00:32:35,666 --> 00:32:40,538
Well, I thought she was
essential to our company.

482
00:32:40,538 --> 00:32:41,887
Well, then,

483
00:32:41,887 --> 00:32:46,954
you should've used your rank to change
the HR system, so you could do that.

484
00:32:46,954 --> 00:32:51,587
That's how a manager should think.

485
00:32:52,510 --> 00:32:58,687
Good grief. My gift to you this time
is that person, Lee Ji Hye,

486
00:32:58,687 --> 00:33:00,698
will be fired.

487
00:33:00,698 --> 00:33:04,854
I hope this gift teaches you something.

488
00:33:16,906 --> 00:33:19,438
I'm sorry. I...

489
00:33:19,438 --> 00:33:20,934
I shouldn't have brought it up.

490
00:33:20,934 --> 00:33:23,726
No, don't be, Mr. Gong. I'm really okay.

491
00:33:23,726 --> 00:33:25,322
What's okay about this?

492
00:33:25,322 --> 00:33:27,287
We're not okay with it either.

493
00:33:32,786 --> 00:33:35,462
Mr. Gong, do you remember this?

494
00:33:35,462 --> 00:33:36,874
What's that?

495
00:33:36,874 --> 00:33:42,487
These are the materials I made
when Ms. Jang first joined us.

496
00:33:43,854 --> 00:33:48,210
You put them on a USB and gave it to me.

497
00:33:48,210 --> 00:33:50,014
You said no matter what happened,

498
00:33:50,014 --> 00:33:54,687
it wouldn't change my value
as the person who made them.

499
00:33:55,834 --> 00:33:58,218
So I'm really okay with this.

500
00:33:58,218 --> 00:34:00,354
A year as a contract worker at Hongsung

501
00:34:00,354 --> 00:34:04,466
is more than enough experience
for other companies to value.

502
00:34:04,466 --> 00:34:06,386
And,

503
00:34:07,038 --> 00:34:11,126
I think I had a great time with a great team.

504
00:34:11,126 --> 00:34:14,754
So please, don't be like this.
I'm truly okay.

505
00:34:16,246 --> 00:34:20,590
Well, after a year at Hongsung,
you've got nothing to be ashamed of.

506
00:34:20,590 --> 00:34:21,654
Of course.

507
00:34:21,654 --> 00:34:24,187
Ji Hye, you'll do well no matter what you do.

508
00:34:24,187 --> 00:34:27,806
Whether you work part-time or go abroad.

509
00:34:27,806 --> 00:34:28,834
Right, Mr. Gong?

510
00:34:28,834 --> 00:34:30,518
Tell me about it.

511
00:34:30,518 --> 00:34:32,321
Speaking of which,

512
00:34:33,018 --> 00:34:37,087
have you ever considered working abroad?

513
00:34:38,870 --> 00:34:42,038
What? Working abroad?

514
00:34:42,038 --> 00:34:45,187
How about Mantua?

515
00:34:47,242 --> 00:34:49,650
Mantua?

516
00:34:49,650 --> 00:34:51,621
Isn't there another way?

517
00:34:53,122 --> 00:34:57,354
I'm confident Ji Hye will become permanent.

518
00:34:57,354 --> 00:34:59,802
But if that doesn't happen,

519
00:34:59,802 --> 00:35:02,374
how about sending her to Mantua?

520
00:35:02,374 --> 00:35:03,610
Mantua?

521
00:35:03,610 --> 00:35:06,726
Yeah, I didn't just put her in charge

522
00:35:06,726 --> 00:35:09,294
of dealing with Mantua for no reason.

523
00:35:09,294 --> 00:35:12,422
Mantua will be sending more goods to Korea,

524
00:35:12,422 --> 00:35:14,810
so they'll probably need
someone dedicated to it.

525
00:35:14,810 --> 00:35:16,666
What do you think?

526
00:35:16,666 --> 00:35:18,554
Mr. Gong.

527
00:35:19,294 --> 00:35:21,018
It's too sudden, right?

528
00:35:21,018 --> 00:35:23,830
Just think about it, and let me know.

529
00:35:23,830 --> 00:35:28,434
But would Mantua even want me?

530
00:35:28,434 --> 00:35:31,154
Just think about whether you'd like it.

531
00:35:32,090 --> 00:35:34,654
If you're willing,

532
00:35:36,318 --> 00:35:38,187
Mr. Sponza said

533
00:35:39,310 --> 00:35:41,487
you'd be more than welcome.

534
00:35:43,778 --> 00:35:46,587
Mr. Gong!

535
00:35:50,598 --> 00:35:52,150
Are you crying again?

536
00:35:52,150 --> 00:35:55,782
What? You don't cry when you're sad,
but you cry when you're happy?

537
00:35:55,782 --> 00:35:59,321
- Forget it.
- That was mean.

538
00:36:00,282 --> 00:36:04,254
Oh, so being pampered
makes you hit people now?

539
00:36:05,378 --> 00:36:10,187
Let's give her some time alone.

540
00:36:11,054 --> 00:36:14,150
- Go cry it out.
- Where are you guys going?

541
00:36:14,150 --> 00:36:16,518
Wait for me!

542
00:36:16,518 --> 00:36:20,558
Ms. Ji Hye is going to Mantua?

543
00:36:20,558 --> 00:36:21,894
Thankfully, she seemed excited about it.

544
00:36:21,894 --> 00:36:25,362
That's great. It's a much bigger company.

545
00:36:25,362 --> 00:36:27,730
Well, she speaks Italian well too.

546
00:36:27,730 --> 00:36:29,954
- Right.
- She'll adjust just fine, right?

547
00:36:29,954 --> 00:36:31,758
Of course.

548
00:36:31,758 --> 00:36:35,102
What is there to worry about?
She'll manage on her own now.

549
00:36:35,102 --> 00:36:37,221
- You think so?
- Yeah.

550
00:36:40,734 --> 00:36:42,390
Hey,

551
00:36:42,390 --> 00:36:46,074
don't you think people have changed?

552
00:36:46,074 --> 00:36:48,394
Why, what's changed?

553
00:36:48,394 --> 00:36:53,762
Well, I can't say for sure that you have.

554
00:36:53,762 --> 00:36:56,354
But I also can't say you haven't.

555
00:36:59,302 --> 00:37:02,334
I don't know about that.

556
00:37:02,334 --> 00:37:04,430
Have I ever said that to you?

557
00:37:04,430 --> 00:37:05,542
What?

558
00:37:05,542 --> 00:37:08,954
Back with Yoo Ji Hyun,
and the whole CGM thing,

559
00:37:09,582 --> 00:37:11,554
did I ever say

560
00:37:12,626 --> 00:37:14,787
thank you?

561
00:37:15,414 --> 00:37:17,298
Thank me?

562
00:37:17,298 --> 00:37:18,998
You?

563
00:37:18,998 --> 00:37:20,922
Did you?

564
00:37:24,390 --> 00:37:26,187
I guess I didn't.

565
00:37:29,654 --> 00:37:31,490
Thanks.

566
00:37:36,386 --> 00:37:38,302
I'm off.

567
00:37:45,126 --> 00:37:46,986
You've changed.

568
00:38:53,654 --> 00:38:58,354
[Daily Routine]

569
00:39:01,606 --> 00:39:03,354
Oh.

570
00:39:06,650 --> 00:39:08,998
Today's beans have a bit of acidity.

571
00:39:08,998 --> 00:39:10,838
Sounds nice.

572
00:39:11,694 --> 00:39:13,170
Well, sir,

573
00:39:13,170 --> 00:39:16,278
you remember the espresso pack
we took with us last time?

574
00:39:16,278 --> 00:39:18,746
Sure, I remember.

575
00:39:18,746 --> 00:39:22,962
The person who drank it said,

576
00:39:22,962 --> 00:39:26,682
"This coffee wasn't made for someone else."

577
00:39:26,682 --> 00:39:28,798
That's quite something.

578
00:39:28,798 --> 00:39:33,534
Because you know,
coffee reflects the person who makes it.

579
00:39:33,534 --> 00:39:36,350
That's fascinating.
That's exactly what she said.

580
00:39:36,350 --> 00:39:39,918
I do make coffee for others.

581
00:39:39,918 --> 00:39:45,454
But I like seeing someone enjoy my coffee,
so in the end, it's for me too.

582
00:39:50,230 --> 00:39:52,222
Well, sir.

583
00:39:52,222 --> 00:39:55,521
This may be a little out of the blue,

584
00:39:57,438 --> 00:39:59,487
but did you perhaps...

585
00:40:00,090 --> 00:40:02,086
Did I perhaps

586
00:40:03,730 --> 00:40:06,146
win the lottery?

587
00:40:06,146 --> 00:40:08,282
You did, didn't you?

588
00:40:08,282 --> 00:40:10,366
Is it that obvious?

589
00:40:10,366 --> 00:40:13,214
I don't know what it is,
but I just had a feeling.

590
00:40:13,214 --> 00:40:15,942
I know, right? I could tell too.

591
00:40:15,942 --> 00:40:17,987
So you already knew.

592
00:40:19,066 --> 00:40:22,121
So what's it like
having all that money in the bank?

593
00:40:23,258 --> 00:40:25,034
I don't know.

594
00:40:27,630 --> 00:40:30,054
I haven't spent a single cent of it,

595
00:40:31,098 --> 00:40:35,187
but it showed me
that so many things could still change.

596
00:40:36,454 --> 00:40:39,110
Then again,

597
00:40:39,110 --> 00:40:41,187
maybe I could

598
00:40:42,330 --> 00:40:45,366
live this same life, even without the money.

599
00:40:46,646 --> 00:40:50,687
I thought nothing had changed at all,
but looking back,

600
00:40:52,450 --> 00:40:54,754
everything had changed.

601
00:40:55,638 --> 00:40:57,490
I guess so.

602
00:40:58,442 --> 00:41:01,187
Just like the taste of coffee
changes every day.

603
00:41:02,502 --> 00:41:04,621
Have a good day.

604
00:41:05,938 --> 00:41:06,990
You too, sir.

605
00:41:06,990 --> 00:41:09,298
Thanks, see you tomorrow.

606
00:41:09,298 --> 00:41:10,334
See you tomorrow.

607
00:41:10,334 --> 00:41:15,087
[Daily Routine]

608
00:41:22,186 --> 00:41:25,306
<i>I'm still the same as yesterday,</i>

609
00:41:25,306 --> 00:41:28,121
<i>living a day that will be
the same as tomorrow.</i>

610
00:41:29,310 --> 00:41:34,487
<i>And just like that, time continues
to pass by, casually, even today.</i>

611
00:42:01,298 --> 00:42:03,354
<i>Door closes.</i>

612
00:42:06,222 --> 00:42:08,182
<i>Door opens.</i>

613
00:42:08,182 --> 00:42:10,138
Oh, my.

614
00:42:10,138 --> 00:42:13,454
- You're here.
- I really thought I was first.

615
00:42:14,426 --> 00:42:15,902
Good morning, good morning.

616
00:42:15,902 --> 00:42:17,094
Ms. Jang!

617
00:42:17,094 --> 00:42:18,442
You're all here early.

618
00:42:18,442 --> 00:42:19,926
Of course.

619
00:42:19,926 --> 00:42:21,230
- Oh, good morning.
- Good morning.

620
00:42:21,230 --> 00:42:24,370
- Good morning.
- Wow, everyone's right on time now.

621
00:42:24,370 --> 00:42:26,494
What's going on?
Why are you two coming in together?

622
00:42:26,494 --> 00:42:28,330
Oh...

623
00:42:29,978 --> 00:42:32,121
<i>Door closes.</i>

624
00:43:02,586 --> 00:43:03,654
Hello.

625
00:43:03,654 --> 00:43:07,554
[Draw Date: August 22, 1st Place Winner,
Congratulations]

626
00:43:13,214 --> 00:43:16,134
Sorry, but our POS system isn't working.

627
00:43:17,818 --> 00:43:19,438
Luckily, I have cash.

628
00:43:19,438 --> 00:43:21,921
Okay, got your 10,000 won.

629
00:43:24,162 --> 00:43:25,858
But you don't have any change, right?

630
00:43:25,858 --> 00:43:27,787
Yeah, you're right.

631
00:43:30,854 --> 00:43:32,821
How would you like me to handle this?
